WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:00:36.495 --> 00:00:38.080
We need to get her out of there!

3
00:00:38.163 --> 00:00:40.666
Stop! The poison could still be inside.

4
00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:42.459
Knox! Stop!

5
00:00:42.543 --> 00:00:43.669
- Listen to me.
- Hey!

6
00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:46.255
We all wanna save her. Okay.
we all wanna save her. but if you open

7
00:00:47.256 --> 00:00:49.216
this door. we have no...

8
00:00:49.967 --> 00:00:52.135
- God! Please. No!
- Everybody. stop!

9
00:00:52.219 --> 00:00:54.346
- We all wanna save her.
- It's stopped!

10
00:00:54.429 --> 00:00:56.515
- Knox. you gotta think--
- The fire stopped!

11
00:00:58.851 --> 00:01:00.853
- We need to open the door.
- No. no. no. no.

12
00:01:00.936 --> 00:01:02.145
No one's ever gone in before.

13
00:01:02.229 --> 00:01:03.230
The lock doesn't release

14
00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:05.232
- for 48 hours after a cleaning.
- She's...

15
00:01:05.315 --> 00:01:06.859
- Forty-eight hours after--
- Juliette's moving!

16
00:01:10.362 --> 00:01:11.530
Fuck 48 hours.

17
00:01:11.613 --> 00:01:12.865
Clear the cafeteria.

18
00:01:12.948 --> 00:01:14.324
We're opening the door.

19
00:01:30.424 --> 00:01:31.633
Move!

20
00:01:36.597 --> 00:01:37.681
Come on!

21
00:01:40.642 --> 00:01:42.895
- Go get the straps. You get her.
- Come on.

22
00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:46.982
- Easy. Easy.
- Get her down.

23
00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:49.735
When she's out.
we'll wrap it right around.

24
00:01:53.405 --> 00:01:54.531
Careful.

25
00:01:59.203 --> 00:02:01.914
Easy. Shirl. Shirl. Be careful.

26
00:02:01.997 --> 00:02:04.708
Hank! Hank!

27
00:02:05.209 --> 00:02:06.668
Get in here. I need help!

28
00:02:06.752 --> 00:02:09.128
Come on. guys. Come on. Let's go. Go!

29
00:02:09.213 --> 00:02:11.673
Teddy. they're coming!

30
00:02:14.051 --> 00:02:16.970
- Move! Clear the way!
- Move 'em back!

31
00:02:17.054 --> 00:02:19.097
Get back. Out of the way!
Make some room! Go!

32
00:02:19.181 --> 00:02:20.516
Clear out! Move! Back it up! Let's go!

33
00:02:20.599 --> 00:02:22.351
Move 'em back! Get back!

34
00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:24.228
- Let's go!
- Get back!

35
00:02:25.103 --> 00:02:27.147
We're going up the stairs. Watch it.

36
00:02:27.231 --> 00:02:29.149
Stay with me. Stay with me.

37
00:02:29.233 --> 00:02:31.777
Come on. Please get out of the way!
Move back! Move!

38
00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:35.364
Go! Back. please stand back. Stand back.

39
00:02:51.296 --> 00:02:53.590
- Get ready.
- Come on.

40
00:02:56.802 --> 00:02:57.970
Get those ropes up.

41
00:02:58.053 --> 00:02:59.680
Come on. Move! Move.

42
00:03:02.432 --> 00:03:03.684
- Hold.
- Pull.

43
00:03:17.364 --> 00:03:18.532
Nice and easy.

44
00:03:20.576 --> 00:03:21.577
Hey!

45
00:03:24.246 --> 00:03:28.917
<i>Hear the bell that rings</i>

46
00:03:29.001 --> 00:03:32.212
<i>It's calling us</i>

47
00:03:32.296 --> 00:03:36.383
<i>To our duty</i>

48
00:03:36.466 --> 00:03:37.467
Move.

49
00:03:37.551 --> 00:03:40.888
<i>Hear the voices sing</i>

50
00:03:40.971 --> 00:03:43.765
<i>So loud and proud</i>

51
00:03:43.849 --> 00:03:44.933
<i>I was told...</i>

52
00:03:45.017 --> 00:03:46.643
<i>Praise freedom's beauty</i>

53
00:03:46.727 --> 00:03:49.188
...the entire Silo was watching

54
00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:52.065
as we were being lowered down.

55
00:03:55.694 --> 00:03:56.695
But what...

56
00:03:58.530 --> 00:03:59.865
Everyone thinks you're dead...

57
00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:04.161
so how did you end up down here?

58
00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:05.996
How the fuck do you think?

59
00:06:02.946 --> 00:06:06.200
<i>Judge Sims.
you and your son must leave the vault.</i>

60
00:06:07.659 --> 00:06:08.952
<i>Camille can stay.</i>

61
00:06:15.667 --> 00:06:16.668
What?

62
00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:32.392
It's okay.

63
00:06:44.655 --> 00:06:45.656
Dad?

64
00:06:51.703 --> 00:06:53.080
Everything is okay.

65
00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:56.041
Mom is safe

66
00:06:57.501 --> 00:07:00.754
and now we're gonna find
a safe place for you and me.

67
00:07:02.589 --> 00:07:03.590
Okay?

68
00:07:27.197 --> 00:07:28.282
Are you okay?

69
00:07:28.365 --> 00:07:31.410
- Is Anthony--
- He's asleep. Finally.

70
00:07:36.748 --> 00:07:37.958
I can't stay long.

71
00:07:41.336 --> 00:07:42.838
But I needed to see you.

72
00:07:45.174 --> 00:07:46.216
What?

73
00:07:47.926 --> 00:07:51.138
What happened in the vault
after we left you?

74
00:07:55.559 --> 00:07:56.727
Rob. I...

75
00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:03.317
I can't talk about that.

76
00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:08.447
What do you mean
you can't talk about that?

77
00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:09.740
Okay...

78
00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:20.542
Did Bernard ever tell you
about what happened in that room?

79
00:08:21.126 --> 00:08:22.461
Or what the voice was?

80
00:08:22.544 --> 00:08:24.379
Or even that there was a voice?

81
00:08:26.548 --> 00:08:28.675
I knew he got instructions in there.

82
00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:31.386
But I didn't know how.

83
00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:37.976
And you won't tell me?

84
00:08:39.811 --> 00:08:41.063
If I could...

85
00:08:46.693 --> 00:08:49.029
We came straight here. I haven't been out.

86
00:08:49.112 --> 00:08:51.490
- I have no idea what's going on.
- It's calm.

87
00:08:52.908 --> 00:08:54.535
Bernard and Juliette came back inside.

88
00:08:56.537 --> 00:08:57.538
Inside?

89
00:08:58.747 --> 00:09:01.416
- How?
- They survived the fire. Barely.

90
00:09:02.584 --> 00:09:03.669
Did the poison get in?

91
00:09:03.752 --> 00:09:04.753
It doesn't look like.

92
00:09:05.379 --> 00:09:07.089
Did anyone try to open the door?

93
00:09:07.172 --> 00:09:08.173
No.

94
00:09:09.508 --> 00:09:13.345
Rob. the rebellion was over the second
she appeared over the top of the hill.

95
00:09:18.267 --> 00:09:20.310
But there are still threats to the Silo.

96
00:09:22.729 --> 00:09:24.565
- Who?
- Bernard Holland.

97
00:09:25.065 --> 00:09:26.066
Lukas Kyle.

98
00:09:27.067 --> 00:09:28.610
And Juliette Nichols.

99
00:09:36.451 --> 00:09:39.621
Are you asking me to take care of it?

100
00:09:43.458 --> 00:09:45.460
I'm telling you there's a problem.

101
00:09:47.462 --> 00:09:50.215
And we both know
this isn't the first time the head of IT...

102
00:09:50.299 --> 00:09:52.050
- I'll take care of it. okay?
- ...has asked you to handle

103
00:09:52.134 --> 00:09:53.135
a problem for them.

104
00:10:00.726 --> 00:10:01.810
What's the concern?

105
00:10:02.728 --> 00:10:04.021
They know things

106
00:10:04.813 --> 00:10:06.231
that could threaten the Silo.

107
00:10:06.315 --> 00:10:07.566
Things I can't know.

108
00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:09.902
That's what you're telling me.

109
00:10:11.486 --> 00:10:12.821
Things I can't know.

110
00:10:18.869 --> 00:10:20.245
What's the order of priority?

111
00:10:22.623 --> 00:10:25.834
Lukas Kyle is the lowest.
When you find him. just make sure

112
00:10:25.918 --> 00:10:27.461
- he doesn't speak to anyone.
- Gag and bag.

113
00:10:27.544 --> 00:10:28.712
Yes.

114
00:10:36.094 --> 00:10:39.264
Juliette and Bernard
are the greatest threat.

115
00:10:45.229 --> 00:10:46.230
Of the two?

116
00:10:46.313 --> 00:10:48.607
Whoever seems likely to talk first.

117
00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:53.820
Honestly. it's too early to tell.

118
00:10:53.904 --> 00:10:55.364
Either of them say anything?

119
00:10:55.447 --> 00:10:57.783
Juliette Nichols is unconscious.

120
00:10:57.866 --> 00:11:00.619
Bernard Holland has made sounds.
not words.

121
00:11:01.119 --> 00:11:03.163
Pain response. He's badly burned.

122
00:11:03.247 --> 00:11:04.289
Nichols?

123
00:11:04.373 --> 00:11:06.834
That suit she was wearing protected her.

124
00:11:07.459 --> 00:11:09.795
Holland's had a lot of burn-through.

125
00:11:10.462 --> 00:11:15.092
Nichols has some burns where the metal
in her collar and wristbands heated up.

126
00:11:15.801 --> 00:11:18.470
And what's your plan
if they don't make it?

127
00:11:18.554 --> 00:11:21.139
We don't have a protocol for any of this.

128
00:11:21.223 --> 00:11:25.310
but I had plastic sheeting
and remains bags placed in their rooms.

129
00:11:25.936 --> 00:11:29.356
I don't believe traditional burial
would be safe. The poison--

130
00:11:29.439 --> 00:11:32.025
- Incineration then.
- Yes.

131
00:11:33.193 --> 00:11:35.612
But the incinerator's 140 levels down.

132
00:11:35.696 --> 00:11:39.324
And if the bodies are contaminated.
and I would have to assume they are.

133
00:11:39.408 --> 00:11:42.244
they'll have to be wrapped in plastic
before being put in the bags.

134
00:11:43.161 --> 00:11:45.038
Protective suits for the porters.

135
00:11:45.122 --> 00:11:46.123
Clear the stairs.

136
00:11:46.915 --> 00:11:47.916
It won't be easy.

137
00:11:50.419 --> 00:11:51.795
Then let's hope they live.

138
00:12:30.417 --> 00:12:31.543
Robert.

139
00:12:33.629 --> 00:12:38.884
I know the voice wants me dead

140
00:12:38.967 --> 00:12:43.263
but... I...

141
00:13:05.661 --> 00:13:08.539
They can kill us at any time.

142
00:13:11.792 --> 00:13:13.418
The whole Silo.

143
00:13:13.919 --> 00:13:17.631
That's what Lukas Kyle found out.

144
00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:19.508
What he told me.

145
00:13:20.717 --> 00:13:21.844
But Juliette...

146
00:13:21.927 --> 00:13:24.096
Juliette knows how to stop it.

147
00:14:10.184 --> 00:14:12.519
- Nice outfit.
- I have a job for you.

148
00:14:18.525 --> 00:14:20.569
You sure you don't wanna go up top?

149
00:14:26.533 --> 00:14:27.534
Be near Medical?

150
00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:29.328
I'm not a doctor.

151
00:14:30.412 --> 00:14:31.914
I can't do anything for her.

152
00:14:34.458 --> 00:14:36.043
Now. down here though.

153
00:14:37.252 --> 00:14:38.962
there's plenty to keep me busy.

154
00:14:40.047 --> 00:14:43.550
Well. there better be
an apartment for us in Mechanical.

155
00:14:43.634 --> 00:14:47.179
because I am not sleeping
in this shithole.

156
00:14:48.972 --> 00:14:50.098
Are you staying?

157
00:14:54.686 --> 00:14:56.104
I was thinking about it.

158
00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:02.402
- I need your help.
- Yeah. and what makes you think

159
00:15:02.486 --> 00:15:04.655
- we'd lift a finger?
- We hate you.

160
00:15:04.738 --> 00:15:06.740
Because my wife is the new head of IT.

161
00:15:06.823 --> 00:15:08.784
and she wants Juliette Nichols dead.

162
00:15:10.285 --> 00:15:13.247
Now. if you help me.
we can stop that from happening.

163
00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:15.541
- You're going against your own wife?
- In five minutes.

164
00:15:15.624 --> 00:15:18.585
I'm meeting with a group of porters
in the incinerator room.

165
00:15:18.669 --> 00:15:19.711
Once they leave.

166
00:15:20.295 --> 00:15:22.339
I have to make a body disappear.

167
00:15:22.422 --> 00:15:24.049
and I need your help to do it.

168
00:15:24.633 --> 00:15:27.761
The Silo has to believe
this person is dead.

169
00:15:28.512 --> 00:15:29.513
Meet me there.

170
00:15:30.347 --> 00:15:31.348
Or don't.

171
00:15:33.141 --> 00:15:35.519
But Juliette's life is on the line.

172
00:15:37.437 --> 00:15:41.358
Who do you want disappeared?

173
00:16:22.816 --> 00:16:25.235
How the fuck are you smiling
after all that?

174
00:16:26.028 --> 00:16:27.946
It's the drugs you gave me.

175
00:16:37.789 --> 00:16:39.791
Our help comes with a condition.

176
00:16:39.875 --> 00:16:42.503
If anything happens to our girl.

177
00:16:42.586 --> 00:16:45.047
we tell Camille that you betrayed her.

178
00:16:46.173 --> 00:16:48.967
And we toss Holland
into the incinerator for real.

179
00:16:50.135 --> 00:16:52.179
- Then let's get moving.
- Hold on.

180
00:16:52.262 --> 00:16:53.555
How can you be so certain

181
00:16:53.639 --> 00:16:57.726
that your wife won't just handle Juliette
while you're down here with us?

182
00:16:57.809 --> 00:17:00.479
Because I made sure
Juliette Nichols is unkillable.

183
00:17:23.001 --> 00:17:25.838
What's going on? Any news yet?

184
00:17:26.922 --> 00:17:28.423
Why were the stairs closed?

185
00:17:28.507 --> 00:17:30.717
The poison got one of them.
They said it wasn't Juliette.

186
00:17:30.801 --> 00:17:33.679
It was Holland.
Had to take him to the incinerator.

187
00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:39.142
If Bernard Holland is dead.
then who's mayor?

188
00:17:40.185 --> 00:17:41.520
What?

189
00:17:42.563 --> 00:17:43.564
Who's mayor?

190
00:17:45.774 --> 00:17:46.984
We need a mayor. don't we?

191
00:17:47.067 --> 00:17:48.694
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

192
00:17:48.777 --> 00:17:52.781
And if we don't choose someone.
then know they'll choose for us.

193
00:17:52.865 --> 00:17:53.866
So. who?

194
00:17:55.450 --> 00:17:56.785
We just had a rebellion.

195
00:17:57.995 --> 00:18:00.247
We need someone we can trust
in charge. right?

196
00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:01.331
Yes.

197
00:18:01.415 --> 00:18:04.084
How about someone
who went out and came back?

198
00:18:04.168 --> 00:18:06.253
Yeah. That's right. That's right.

199
00:18:06.336 --> 00:18:09.423
Hell. I say Juliette Nichols
for mayor. Yeah?

200
00:18:09.506 --> 00:18:11.800
- Yeah. Juliette!
- Yeah. Juliette Nichols for mayor!

201
00:18:11.884 --> 00:18:15.637
- Yeah! Juliette!
- Yeah! Juliette Nichols for mayor!

202
00:18:15.721 --> 00:18:18.640
- Juliette for mayor! Juliette for mayor!
- Juliette for mayor! Juliette for mayor!

203
00:18:19.224 --> 00:18:23.478
Juliette for mayor!
Juliette for mayor! Juliette for mayor!

204
00:18:28.984 --> 00:18:31.486
It smells like it's burning.

205
00:18:31.570 --> 00:18:33.405
It's not burning.

206
00:18:34.865 --> 00:18:37.659
Well. you burnt it last time.

207
00:18:37.743 --> 00:18:38.744
Yeah. well.

208
00:18:40.454 --> 00:18:43.373
Maybe you're a little sensitive
to things being burnt.

209
00:18:43.457 --> 00:18:44.499
Did you think of that?

210
00:18:46.293 --> 00:18:48.837
Yeah. I shouldn't be so funny. I'm sorry.

211
00:18:53.258 --> 00:18:55.219
Little hot. still.

212
00:19:00.807 --> 00:19:02.184
You know. I got a question.

213
00:19:04.436 --> 00:19:06.438
All these other silos.

214
00:19:07.314 --> 00:19:09.149
Are they all like ours?

215
00:19:10.609 --> 00:19:11.610
I think so.

216
00:19:12.402 --> 00:19:14.071
So do they all have radios?

217
00:19:15.030 --> 00:19:16.031
They do.

218
00:19:17.199 --> 00:19:18.534
So how come we haven't heard them?

219
00:19:18.617 --> 00:19:21.954
Because you're listening
to the wrong signal.

220
00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:24.831
Bring me a radio

221
00:19:25.874 --> 00:19:29.253
and I'll show you what I know.

222
00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:36.885
- Is it done?
- Mayor Juliette Nichols

223
00:19:36.969 --> 00:19:39.346
took the oath of office
from her hospital bed.

224
00:19:40.097 --> 00:19:41.932
They're discharging her this week.

225
00:19:42.015 --> 00:19:46.311
Which means they've started her
on the forgetting drugs.

226
00:19:46.895 --> 00:19:48.272
They need to make sure that

227
00:19:49.064 --> 00:19:52.776
she doesn't remember
what she saw in Silo 17.

228
00:19:53.402 --> 00:19:56.029
If she's on 'em too long.
she'll forget everything.

229
00:19:56.113 --> 00:19:58.407
Then we gotta get her off of those drugs.

230
00:19:58.490 --> 00:20:00.075
That's gonna be hard to do.

231
00:20:00.158 --> 00:20:02.286
Camille's got her on a tight leash.

232
00:20:02.369 --> 00:20:06.373
Is there no way of reversing it?
Of getting her memories back?

233
00:20:06.456 --> 00:20:09.084
There's talk in <i>The Order</i>.

234
00:20:09.168 --> 00:20:10.586
What's <i>The Order</i>?

235
00:20:10.669 --> 00:20:11.670
<i>The Order</i> is...

236
00:20:11.753 --> 00:20:13.755
It's like the Pact.

237
00:20:14.923 --> 00:20:18.468
but just for the head of IT
and their shadow.

238
00:20:19.178 --> 00:20:24.308
It gives instructions
on what to do when things go wrong.

239
00:20:25.851 --> 00:20:30.480
When it describes the use
of the forgetting drugs on people.

240
00:20:31.607 --> 00:20:34.318
it says it's essential

241
00:20:35.194 --> 00:20:38.864
to keep them from artifacts
from their past.

242
00:20:40.032 --> 00:20:44.077
as these artifacts can trigger memories.

243
00:20:44.161 --> 00:20:47.331
So. that's why you had your goons
looking for relics all of these years.

244
00:20:47.414 --> 00:20:49.374
I never knew about <i>The Order</i>.

245
00:20:49.958 --> 00:20:52.794
But the Pact says a lot
about what's outlawed.

246
00:20:54.296 --> 00:20:55.797
But never said why.

247
00:21:02.054 --> 00:21:03.222
I'd better get started.

248
00:21:03.305 --> 00:21:04.640
Where are you going?

249
00:21:04.723 --> 00:21:06.350
If we're gonna get Nichols off
those drugs.

250
00:21:06.433 --> 00:21:07.768
there's someone I need to see.

251
00:21:08.352 --> 00:21:09.853
Only hope it's not too late.

252
00:21:26.245 --> 00:21:27.246
Baby?

253
00:21:54.314 --> 00:21:56.024
You left your door open.

254
00:21:59.027 --> 00:22:00.696
Does this never end?

255
00:22:00.779 --> 00:22:03.699
I need you to get these pills
to Amy Hansen.

256
00:22:03.782 --> 00:22:06.660
She's the nurse attending Mayor Nichols.

257
00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:10.080
Regina. look at me.

258
00:22:12.541 --> 00:22:14.626
I don't know her from a bar of soap.

259
00:22:15.794 --> 00:22:17.337
Why would she take anything from me?

260
00:22:17.421 --> 00:22:19.756
I will send you to an intermediary.

261
00:22:19.840 --> 00:22:22.050
Someone who does know Amy Hansen.

262
00:22:23.510 --> 00:22:26.054
- Who?
- You will tell this intermediary

263
00:22:26.138 --> 00:22:27.598
that at some point.

264
00:22:28.182 --> 00:22:31.185
Hansen will need to replace
Nichols's vitamins with these.

265
00:22:34.396 --> 00:22:36.440
What's in those? Poison?

266
00:22:36.523 --> 00:22:39.234
- It's just sugar.
- What's in the pills she's getting now?

267
00:22:39.318 --> 00:22:41.737
It's best if you only know
what you need to know.

268
00:22:42.529 --> 00:22:44.031
Will you do this?

269
00:22:48.493 --> 00:22:49.870
Do I have a choice?

270
00:22:49.953 --> 00:22:50.954
You do.

271
00:22:51.496 --> 00:22:53.540
And what happens if I say no?

272
00:22:53.624 --> 00:22:56.627
My family suddenly get hauled to Judicial?

273
00:22:56.710 --> 00:22:59.630
My friend bumps into a raider
and suddenly goes over the rail?

274
00:22:59.713 --> 00:23:01.256
None of that happens.

275
00:23:04.843 --> 00:23:08.305
- I don't understand.
- I'm just asking if you will help.

276
00:23:24.905 --> 00:23:27.699
I hear your wife's the new head of IT.

277
00:23:29.701 --> 00:23:30.786
She know about this?

278
00:23:31.620 --> 00:23:32.913
She does not.

279
00:23:40.379 --> 00:23:41.380
Okay.

280
00:23:47.386 --> 00:23:50.055
Now. I'll need you
to start trading in relics again.

281
00:23:50.639 --> 00:23:52.349
I know. I know.

282
00:23:53.308 --> 00:23:55.894
Look. anything that belonged to Nichols.

283
00:23:55.978 --> 00:23:58.564
Raiders and agents.
they will look the other way.

284
00:23:59.273 --> 00:24:02.401
A lot of her stuff's been scooped up
by those women who dress like her.

285
00:24:02.985 --> 00:24:04.278
I'll need something to trade.

286
00:24:04.778 --> 00:24:05.779
Like what?

287
00:24:05.863 --> 00:24:07.281
Something small.

288
00:24:07.364 --> 00:24:08.949
Maybe with her name on it.

289
00:24:09.825 --> 00:24:10.868
Her sheriff's badge.

290
00:24:12.828 --> 00:24:14.288
Ten of them should be enough.

291
00:24:15.581 --> 00:24:17.749
Where did you get the badges?

292
00:24:17.833 --> 00:24:20.919
There's a craftsman in the marketplace
who owed me.

293
00:24:21.003 --> 00:24:23.380
You mean he's afraid of you.

294
00:24:23.463 --> 00:24:27.426
Fifty silos. all given the same radio.

295
00:24:28.135 --> 00:24:30.429
Each silo using a different frequency.

296
00:24:32.681 --> 00:24:34.683
What did you say they were called again?

297
00:24:35.475 --> 00:24:39.771
In the book. it calls them channels.

298
00:24:39.855 --> 00:24:41.815
Channels. that's right. channels.

299
00:24:42.316 --> 00:24:47.863
So. I've tuned this radio
to another silo's channel.

300
00:24:47.946 --> 00:24:50.657
so that. in here.
we can talk without anyone hearing.

301
00:24:51.325 --> 00:24:57.080
Silo 1 monitors
all of the active frequencies.

302
00:24:57.164 --> 00:24:59.208
so use it sparingly.

303
00:24:59.791 --> 00:25:01.335
And in code.

304
00:25:01.960 --> 00:25:04.463
Okay. well.
I gotta go and get some more food.

305
00:25:05.005 --> 00:25:06.715
His appetite's returning.

306
00:25:13.263 --> 00:25:14.681
You headed up soon?

307
00:25:14.765 --> 00:25:18.060
My quarantine doesn't officially end
until noon.

308
00:25:18.644 --> 00:25:20.521
What are you gonna tell your wife?

309
00:25:20.604 --> 00:25:23.232
She told me to take care of
whoever might talk first.

310
00:25:23.315 --> 00:25:24.358
That was you.

311
00:25:26.193 --> 00:25:29.029
You sure you don't want
to get Nichols off the drugs now?

312
00:25:29.530 --> 00:25:34.159
We can't let it happen too soon
after you return from quarantine--

313
00:25:34.243 --> 00:25:35.494
The longer we wait.

314
00:25:35.577 --> 00:25:40.707
- the more difficult it'll become.
- We can't risk losing you. Robert.

315
00:25:41.375 --> 00:25:44.753
You are indispensable.

316
00:25:48.131 --> 00:25:51.051
I'm impressed

317
00:25:52.261 --> 00:25:55.138
with how you've handled.

318
00:25:56.765 --> 00:25:58.016
well. everything.

319
00:25:59.476 --> 00:26:01.311
You would have been a great shadow...

320
00:26:03.397 --> 00:26:05.816
but I am glad I didn't give you the job.

321
00:26:07.234 --> 00:26:08.735
Being head of IT...

322
00:26:11.029 --> 00:26:12.823
is a brutal.

323
00:26:14.408 --> 00:26:18.954
thankless. impossible task.

324
00:26:21.456 --> 00:26:24.126
It's no better for the shadow.

325
00:26:26.795 --> 00:26:33.468
The things that fucking voice
in the vault made me do.

326
00:26:38.974 --> 00:26:40.058
I thought...

327
00:26:42.102 --> 00:26:44.354
the greatest risk

328
00:26:44.438 --> 00:26:49.359
was from some fool
trying to open the door.

329
00:26:56.200 --> 00:26:58.493
Camille has it far worse.

330
00:27:00.913 --> 00:27:04.208
They had to tell her about the Safeguard.

331
00:27:06.043 --> 00:27:12.549
and she can't speak about it to anyone.

332
00:27:16.762 --> 00:27:18.055
I imagine...

333
00:27:20.265 --> 00:27:23.894
she's burning alive from the inside.

334
00:27:26.647 --> 00:27:29.274
<i>I went back up. and we waited.</i>

335
00:27:30.067 --> 00:27:32.986
Maybe too long
considering how much you forgot.

336
00:27:33.070 --> 00:27:37.366
So when I met you in the pump room.
you were gonna bring me down here?

337
00:27:37.449 --> 00:27:40.702
You were going to talk to me on the radio.

338
00:27:40.786 --> 00:27:45.541
We didn't want anyone coming here.
but you and your friend fucked that up.

339
00:27:50.295 --> 00:27:54.550
That dream you had of you
and Bernard in the air lock.

340
00:27:56.969 --> 00:27:58.011
- Yeah?
- That...

341
00:27:58.804 --> 00:28:00.055
That wasn't a dream.

342
00:28:00.764 --> 00:28:01.890
It was a memory.

343
00:28:02.683 --> 00:28:03.809
It happened.

344
00:28:07.688 --> 00:28:09.481
No. no. wait. you...

345
00:28:13.652 --> 00:28:15.946
- Did you... You had a gun?
- Yes.

346
00:28:16.029 --> 00:28:19.408
And you were gonna go out to die. right?

347
00:28:19.491 --> 00:28:20.742
Yes.

348
00:28:20.826 --> 00:28:22.244
And then what happened?

349
00:28:24.413 --> 00:28:26.081
You happened. Juliette.

350
00:28:26.915 --> 00:28:32.087
I said to you.
"They can kill us all at any time."

351
00:28:33.130 --> 00:28:36.717
And you said. "Maybe not."

352
00:28:38.093 --> 00:28:40.554
What did you mean by maybe not?

353
00:28:44.141 --> 00:28:45.809
I don't remember. I can't.

354
00:28:47.144 --> 00:28:49.771
It's okay. we have a plan.

355
00:28:55.944 --> 00:28:57.863
Come on. come on. come on.

356
00:28:57.946 --> 00:29:00.115
The first time I did that.
I just about shit my pants.

357
00:29:01.200 --> 00:29:02.993
How come you're not freaking the fuck out?

358
00:29:03.076 --> 00:29:05.370
What? I am. okay? Just in the mines.
you learn not to show it.

359
00:29:05.454 --> 00:29:07.414
Yeah. so the big bad bullies
don't pick on you?

360
00:29:07.497 --> 00:29:09.666
No. 'cause there's no point.

361
00:29:10.959 --> 00:29:12.920
Let's go. Come on.

362
00:29:16.298 --> 00:29:17.799
Fifty silos?

363
00:29:19.051 --> 00:29:20.260
Yeah.

364
00:29:21.303 --> 00:29:23.639
- Are they all like us?
- Far as I know.

365
00:29:23.722 --> 00:29:25.098
But there's one that can fucking kill us?

366
00:29:25.182 --> 00:29:26.225
Yes.

367
00:29:28.852 --> 00:29:32.439
You've known about this for months.
and you're only telling us now?

368
00:29:32.523 --> 00:29:33.774
I couldn't tell you.

369
00:29:33.857 --> 00:29:35.359
Just like you can't tell anyone.

370
00:29:36.151 --> 00:29:37.486
Listen. we're safe here.

371
00:29:38.320 --> 00:29:41.490
but if anyone speaks about this openly.
then they will kill us.

372
00:29:42.074 --> 00:29:44.034
How would that actually happen?

373
00:29:44.117 --> 00:29:46.203
Well. if I knew that.
we wouldn't need Juliette.

374
00:29:46.286 --> 00:29:48.205
- Why would they kill us?
- I haven't a clue.

375
00:29:48.288 --> 00:29:49.998
All I know is that they could.

376
00:29:50.082 --> 00:29:51.333
That's all I need to know.

377
00:29:51.416 --> 00:29:53.168
Listen.

378
00:29:54.044 --> 00:29:57.589
the reason I'm telling you this
and scaring the shit out of you

379
00:29:59.299 --> 00:30:00.759
is that I need your help.

380
00:30:01.844 --> 00:30:05.556
Juliette's visit to the digger void
was unanticipated.

381
00:30:05.639 --> 00:30:08.892
so it means
Camille might go down there looking.

382
00:30:08.976 --> 00:30:13.647
and there's something down there
that we can't let her find.

383
00:30:16.400 --> 00:30:19.695
I have to move it. and it's not light.

384
00:30:21.113 --> 00:30:23.240
How much does it weigh?

385
00:30:23.323 --> 00:30:27.244
About 250. and it's a pain in the ass.

386
00:30:31.957 --> 00:30:33.667
You gotta be fucking kidding me?

387
00:30:33.750 --> 00:30:35.252
He's alive?

388
00:30:38.213 --> 00:30:41.216
- You slept there?
- Wouldn't call it sleep.

389
00:30:42.384 --> 00:30:44.928
There's a hostel three levels up.

390
00:30:45.512 --> 00:30:47.890
Everything all right
with your home life. Sheriff?

391
00:30:49.975 --> 00:30:52.186
I told you I needed
to see you immediately.

392
00:30:53.687 --> 00:30:55.355
This is not immediately.

393
00:30:57.107 --> 00:30:58.108
Really?

394
00:30:59.067 --> 00:31:02.696
After all we've been through.
you're gonna play the sheriff card?

395
00:31:02.779 --> 00:31:04.198
It's not a card.

396
00:31:05.157 --> 00:31:06.283
It's a badge.

397
00:31:06.366 --> 00:31:08.493
And yes. I am.

398
00:31:08.577 --> 00:31:09.786
Okay. Paul.

399
00:31:10.370 --> 00:31:12.372
I came as soon as I could.

400
00:31:12.456 --> 00:31:15.834
If Orla isn't here.
then I don't know where she is.

401
00:31:15.918 --> 00:31:17.794
She's in the morgue on 62.

402
00:31:20.506 --> 00:31:22.216
- What?
- She was murdered.

403
00:31:25.719 --> 00:31:26.720
Sorry.

404
00:31:28.096 --> 00:31:29.848
but I need to keep moving on this.

405
00:31:29.932 --> 00:31:32.017
- I have to ask you--
- It's my fault.

406
00:31:36.980 --> 00:31:38.190
It's my fault.

407
00:31:42.861 --> 00:31:44.863
- All right.
- Hey. you know...

408
00:31:44.947 --> 00:31:45.948
Come on.

409
00:31:48.784 --> 00:31:51.995
Can you light a match. man?
I can't see anything.

410
00:31:52.079 --> 00:31:53.956
Yeah. I just want you to know I don't have
an unlimited supply--

411
00:31:54.039 --> 00:31:55.332
I know you don't have it. I know.

412
00:31:55.415 --> 00:31:58.043
- You wanna fall down the shaft?
- No. I don't wanna fall down the shaft.

413
00:31:58.126 --> 00:31:59.545
Okay. Light a match.

414
00:31:59.628 --> 00:32:00.671
Fine. I'm gonna.

415
00:32:00.754 --> 00:32:02.923
When I get to the bottom of the stairs.
I will turn on the light.

416
00:32:03.006 --> 00:32:04.383
All right. good.

417
00:32:05.843 --> 00:32:07.886
What the actual fuck!

418
00:32:08.595 --> 00:32:11.431
You need to be very. very quiet.

419
00:32:11.515 --> 00:32:14.184
- Uh-huh. We can. Yes. Yeah.
- We can do that.

420
00:32:18.939 --> 00:32:20.023
Wait a minute.

421
00:32:20.774 --> 00:32:22.317
Why are they here?

422
00:32:22.401 --> 00:32:24.278
They know too much to be anywhere else.

423
00:32:33.871 --> 00:32:35.289
Do you have the relics?

424
00:34:11.760 --> 00:34:12.803
Anything?

425
00:34:18.516 --> 00:34:20.435
No. I mean. I know. I know...

426
00:34:20.518 --> 00:34:23.230
I know what these things are and I...

427
00:34:23.313 --> 00:34:24.940
I recognize them. I just don't...

428
00:34:27.025 --> 00:34:28.025
It's okay.

429
00:34:28.110 --> 00:34:30.112
Nothing about how to stop them
from killing us?

430
00:34:30.904 --> 00:34:33.031
I'm sorry. Who can do what now?

431
00:34:34.366 --> 00:34:37.244
We really need you
to be quiet right now. Please.

432
00:34:37.870 --> 00:34:39.329
You know about the Safeguard then?

433
00:34:40.121 --> 00:34:41.456
- Yes.
- Okay.

434
00:34:41.540 --> 00:34:43.417
So. you know that they
can kill us at any time?

435
00:34:43.500 --> 00:34:45.127
Yeah. we know that. but I don't know why.

436
00:34:45.210 --> 00:34:46.962
and I can't fucking remember anything.

437
00:34:48.172 --> 00:34:53.342
Okay. how is the box supposed to help?

438
00:34:53.427 --> 00:34:57.306
The hope is things from her past
might jump-start her memory.

439
00:35:01.101 --> 00:35:02.186
Right. Okay. Sorry.

440
00:35:07.941 --> 00:35:09.484
I mean they're toys.

441
00:35:09.568 --> 00:35:10.944
I got everything I could.

442
00:35:11.028 --> 00:35:14.031
What I'm trying to say
is that maybe if we got something

443
00:35:14.114 --> 00:35:16.491
that's more relevant
to when this all started.

444
00:35:17.242 --> 00:35:19.077
Right? Hey. when we met.

445
00:35:19.161 --> 00:35:22.831
yeah. you were asking the big questions:
Why we're here. What it's all for.

446
00:35:22.915 --> 00:35:24.124
But. really.

447
00:35:25.542 --> 00:35:28.045
all you were interested in
was what happened to George.

448
00:35:29.129 --> 00:35:31.006
When I went down
to the bottom of the Silo.

449
00:35:31.089 --> 00:35:33.258
I found a tunnel that led to a door.

450
00:35:33.342 --> 00:35:36.720
and at the door a voice said

451
00:35:36.803 --> 00:35:38.847
that only three people
had ever been there.

452
00:35:38.931 --> 00:35:43.602
Salvador Quinn. Mary Meadows.
and George Wilkins.

453
00:35:43.685 --> 00:35:45.312
On the hard drive. There was a...

454
00:35:45.395 --> 00:35:48.232
There was a guy who was talking to you.
and Danny said that that guy was George.

455
00:35:48.315 --> 00:35:50.901
Did he say anything
about how to stop the Safeguard?

456
00:35:50.984 --> 00:35:54.238
No. No. He said a bunch of mushy shit.
I don't know.

457
00:35:54.321 --> 00:35:57.533
And the he said something
about... that he found a door.

458
00:35:57.616 --> 00:36:00.118
He wanted to find that
door for a long time.

459
00:36:00.202 --> 00:36:02.162
I'm sorry. You also knew George?

460
00:36:02.746 --> 00:36:04.706
- Yeah.
- Well. have you found anything

461
00:36:04.790 --> 00:36:06.708
that belonged to him
that maybe means something to her?

462
00:36:06.792 --> 00:36:09.127
The thing I wanted to get wasn't gettable.

463
00:36:09.920 --> 00:36:12.172
- Why?
- The watch.

464
00:36:13.882 --> 00:36:15.133
George gave you a watch.

465
00:36:15.217 --> 00:36:16.343
I know the watch.

466
00:36:16.426 --> 00:36:17.678
Sorry. Why was it un-gettable?

467
00:36:17.761 --> 00:36:20.514
It was taken from her
before she was sent out to clean.

468
00:36:21.765 --> 00:36:23.183
Bernard gave it to your father.

469
00:36:23.267 --> 00:36:24.977
He was wearing it when
he blew up the stairs.

470
00:36:25.060 --> 00:36:28.021
No. He wasn't wearing it.

471
00:36:28.105 --> 00:36:29.815
He gave it to somebody else.

472
00:36:36.572 --> 00:36:39.324
Your dad wanted me
to give this back to you

473
00:36:39.408 --> 00:36:41.451
if I ever saw you again.

474
00:36:43.036 --> 00:36:44.121
But...

475
00:36:45.414 --> 00:36:48.375
But you weren't really you
when you came back.

476
00:36:48.458 --> 00:36:50.794
- So. I hung on to it.
- Right.

477
00:36:53.839 --> 00:36:54.882
There's something...

478
00:36:54.965 --> 00:36:56.925
There's something I gotta tell you. Jules.

479
00:36:58.844 --> 00:36:59.928
What?

480
00:37:00.971 --> 00:37:03.390
- Can...
- They can hear.

481
00:37:03.473 --> 00:37:05.267
No. This is just for you.

482
00:37:10.063 --> 00:37:11.857
- Come over here.
- Yeah.

483
00:37:36.548 --> 00:37:41.178
He told me to tell you that he loved you.

484
00:37:44.264 --> 00:37:45.891
He wanted you to keep fighting.

485
00:37:47.309 --> 00:37:49.978
- And never stop being yourself because...
- Okay.

486
00:37:52.981 --> 00:37:54.733
"Because she's perfect.

487
00:37:56.485 --> 00:37:58.153
Exactly as she is."

488
00:38:27.933 --> 00:38:30.018
<i>This must have taken you hours.</i>

489
00:38:53.208 --> 00:38:54.334
George.

490
00:38:57.796 --> 00:38:58.964
Are you okay?

491
00:39:01.133 --> 00:39:02.467
Is there anything else?

492
00:39:07.556 --> 00:39:09.016
Then it's time we head up.

493
00:39:09.725 --> 00:39:13.187
I don't know what we're going to say.
but we've been gone too long.

494
00:39:13.270 --> 00:39:16.690
- Camille's going to--
- Did he have anything else? Any...

495
00:39:17.774 --> 00:39:19.359
Do you have anything?

496
00:39:20.027 --> 00:39:21.486
- Not that we know of.
- No?

497
00:39:26.325 --> 00:39:28.118
Hey. We have to go.

498
00:39:33.040 --> 00:39:34.458
We will keep looking.

499
00:39:36.001 --> 00:39:38.086
Critical Supply can only be accessed

500
00:39:38.170 --> 00:39:40.672
by the head of Supply or their shadow.

501
00:40:20.838 --> 00:40:22.881
Every item that goes out of here

502
00:40:22.965 --> 00:40:25.634
requires three different kinds
of approval.

503
00:40:25.717 --> 00:40:29.304
And the head or their shadow
to be in attendance

504
00:40:29.388 --> 00:40:30.806
when those items are pulled.

505
00:40:34.977 --> 00:40:38.188
Critical Supply contains things
that were loaded in here

506
00:40:38.272 --> 00:40:40.023
when the Silo first began.

507
00:40:42.025 --> 00:40:45.112
The kind of things
that we can't make more of.

508
00:40:46.572 --> 00:40:47.990
That's why it's called critical.

509
00:40:49.199 --> 00:40:50.784
You get what that means?

510
00:40:51.994 --> 00:40:54.955
When we run out. we're out.

511
00:40:55.914 --> 00:40:57.040
Exactly.

512
00:41:00.752 --> 00:41:02.212
Pick up one of those boxes.

513
00:41:17.853 --> 00:41:18.937
I'll give you a hand.

514
00:41:31.867 --> 00:41:32.951
Now. pick up that one.

515
00:41:52.262 --> 00:41:58.185
We keep the empty boxes to stop anyone
who might get in here from doing the math.

516
00:42:00.062 --> 00:42:05.817
The amount of panic it will cause
if people found out...

517
00:42:09.988 --> 00:42:11.156
Found out what?

518
00:42:14.701 --> 00:42:16.286
How much time we have left.

519
00:42:19.414 --> 00:42:21.208
Let's get this shit done.

520
00:42:21.291 --> 00:42:23.544
Miss Campbell. Mr. Knox.

521
00:42:29.174 --> 00:42:31.051
You're gonna pull me up?

522
00:42:31.134 --> 00:42:32.344
Unless we let go.

523
00:42:44.231 --> 00:42:46.149
You're enjoying my discomfort?

524
00:42:49.111 --> 00:42:53.282
For 25 years.
I did what I was told I had to do

525
00:42:53.365 --> 00:42:56.243
- to keep the Silo safe.
- So what? You expect us to forgive you?

526
00:42:56.827 --> 00:42:58.287
For murdering the judge?

527
00:42:58.370 --> 00:43:00.038
Blaming it on us?

528
00:43:00.122 --> 00:43:02.916
Telling the entire Silo to kill us?

529
00:43:03.709 --> 00:43:05.377
No. I don't.

530
00:43:06.170 --> 00:43:07.254
I don't.

531
00:43:13.468 --> 00:43:17.806
You both were caught in the middle
of an unfortunate circumstance.

532
00:43:19.308 --> 00:43:20.350
So.

533
00:43:21.852 --> 00:43:23.187
when you pull me up.

534
00:43:24.229 --> 00:43:27.399
I wouldn't be surprised or offended

535
00:43:28.775 --> 00:43:31.028
if you just let me go.

536
00:44:11.610 --> 00:44:12.861
What does this mean?

537
00:44:16.573 --> 00:44:20.953
Twenty years ago
we had 70 years of light bulbs left.

538
00:44:21.745 --> 00:44:25.040
Just before I moved to Mechanical.
about three months ago.

539
00:44:25.582 --> 00:44:27.292
we were down to 50 years.

540
00:44:27.376 --> 00:44:31.839
- Okay. So--
- But a month ago. I did a check.

541
00:44:32.339 --> 00:44:36.718
and I found out that the theft we've been
dealing with in Supply for years

542
00:44:36.802 --> 00:44:39.471
was also happening in Critical Supply.

543
00:44:39.555 --> 00:44:41.390
and that's when I made Orla my shadow.

544
00:44:41.473 --> 00:44:43.475
Because you didn't trust Glenda?

545
00:44:43.559 --> 00:44:47.062
Glenda is capable but prickly.

546
00:44:47.771 --> 00:44:50.482
But Orla. she's from a long line
of Supply-siders.

547
00:44:50.566 --> 00:44:56.446
so I knew I could trust her with the job
and with something else.

548
00:45:01.285 --> 00:45:04.788
You asked her to help you find
who was stealing in Critical Supply.

549
00:45:08.000 --> 00:45:10.252
And you think that's why she got killed?

550
00:45:20.762 --> 00:45:22.055
Carla...

551
00:45:24.266 --> 00:45:26.351
If we can't find those light bulbs.

552
00:45:27.936 --> 00:45:29.396
how long do we have?

553
00:45:30.314 --> 00:45:31.315
With what we got left...

554
00:45:33.901 --> 00:45:34.943
two years.

555
00:45:36.403 --> 00:45:40.240
After that. we won't be able to replace
the ones that go out on the farms.

556
00:45:40.324 --> 00:45:43.243
And when they go. our food goes.

557
00:45:43.827 --> 00:45:44.870
So.

558
00:45:45.829 --> 00:45:47.873
it's only a matter of time

559
00:45:47.956 --> 00:45:49.333
before we die

560
00:45:50.792 --> 00:45:52.211
in the dark.

561
00:45:54.922 --> 00:45:57.049
What do you think Camille is gonna do
when we get there?

562
00:46:00.302 --> 00:46:01.345
I don't know.

563
00:46:03.722 --> 00:46:06.225
Maybe you should put me in handcuffs
and make a scene out of it.

564
00:46:08.143 --> 00:46:09.520
She wanted you dead.

565
00:46:10.229 --> 00:46:11.855
Handcuffs aren't gonna cut it.

566
00:46:15.359 --> 00:46:17.861
Well. you know. one big shove.
and I'll go over the rail.

567
00:46:17.945 --> 00:46:19.530
I mean. we have enough time. right?

568
00:46:19.613 --> 00:46:20.781
Nah.

569
00:46:22.199 --> 00:46:23.242
I'm tired.

570
00:46:34.002 --> 00:46:36.088
- You okay?
- Yeah.

571
00:46:38.215 --> 00:46:39.424
I'm sorry.

572
00:46:42.219 --> 00:46:43.303
There's...

573
00:46:46.765 --> 00:46:48.851
Something I gotta tell you...

574
00:46:52.479 --> 00:46:54.690
It might not be anything. but...

575
00:46:56.692 --> 00:46:58.777
since that night
you went into my apartment.

576
00:47:00.028 --> 00:47:01.864
something changed in my boy.

577
00:47:05.534 --> 00:47:06.869
Maybe in me too.

578
00:47:07.452 --> 00:47:10.539
- Okay. Look. I'm sorry. I've said...
- It's not that.

579
00:47:10.622 --> 00:47:11.790
- I don't know why...
- I didn't bring...

580
00:47:11.874 --> 00:47:13.834
I didn't bring it up for that reason.

581
00:47:16.712 --> 00:47:18.338
And I gave him something.

582
00:47:19.256 --> 00:47:21.049
Told him it'd keep him safe.

583
00:47:21.800 --> 00:47:23.719
And it kinda became our thing.

584
00:47:26.889 --> 00:47:28.599
Like a secret between us.

585
00:47:30.475 --> 00:47:32.811
And the more Bernard talked
about artifacts

586
00:47:32.895 --> 00:47:35.063
being able to trigger someone's memory.

587
00:47:35.147 --> 00:47:40.068
the more I convinced myself that
this thing will help my son remember me...

588
00:47:42.196 --> 00:47:44.031
if Camille released the vitamin D.

589
00:47:45.949 --> 00:47:49.244
Like it was gonna perform
some kind of magic or something.

590
00:47:53.373 --> 00:47:55.083
But it wasn't mine to keep.

591
00:47:56.502 --> 00:47:58.128
It was yours.

592
00:48:03.383 --> 00:48:05.093
George gave it to you.

593
00:48:19.858 --> 00:48:20.943
Was it important?

594
00:48:26.740 --> 00:48:30.994
And in a world filled with a million
unknowns. it is possible that this watch...

595
00:48:31.078 --> 00:48:33.330
and crazy relics like these...

596
00:48:33.413 --> 00:48:35.374
- George.
- ...are the key to answering

597
00:48:35.457 --> 00:48:36.875
- the Silo's biggest questions.
- George.

598
00:48:36.959 --> 00:48:39.127
<i>...what's left
of the machine that dug the Silo.</i>

599
00:48:39.211 --> 00:48:41.046
You would've killed everyone in the Silo.

600
00:48:41.129 --> 00:48:43.924
<i>What silo? There's 50.</i>

601
00:48:44.007 --> 00:48:45.300
It's a pipe.

602
00:48:45.384 --> 00:48:47.636
- The Safeguard is a pipe.
- Why did they have to cap it?

603
00:48:47.719 --> 00:48:49.429
It had poison in it.

604
00:48:49.513 --> 00:48:53.141
Enough poison to kill everybody.
All 10.000 people.

605
00:48:58.188 --> 00:48:59.439
I remember.

606
00:49:07.656 --> 00:49:09.908
There's poison in a pipe.

607
00:49:09.992 --> 00:49:12.202
It comes from outside the Silo.

608
00:49:12.286 --> 00:49:14.955
They capped it in 17.
They fucking capped it.

609
00:49:15.038 --> 00:49:16.331
Where does it come in?

610
00:49:19.626 --> 00:49:20.669
I don't know.

611
00:49:21.712 --> 00:49:23.172
I don't know.
I have to talk to the others.

612
00:49:23.255 --> 00:49:24.423
Go.

613
00:50:00.918 --> 00:50:03.253
So. I'm at the call center.
and I get a call.

614
00:50:03.837 --> 00:50:06.590
which is weird 'cause I didn't know you
could get incoming calls in that system.

615
00:50:06.673 --> 00:50:08.300
But Sam did two years with the NSA.

616
00:50:08.383 --> 00:50:10.177
- so he knows shit.
- He's got magic beans. Yeah.

617
00:50:10.260 --> 00:50:11.261
What did he say?

618
00:50:11.345 --> 00:50:14.306
Who's the number one advocate
for AI control

619
00:50:14.389 --> 00:50:15.724
who also happens to fund the clinic

620
00:50:15.807 --> 00:50:17.768
where my sister's trying
to rebuild her memory?

621
00:50:17.851 --> 00:50:19.353
- Per Stensen.
- Wanna take a guess

622
00:50:19.436 --> 00:50:22.814
at where Per Stensen was the night
of Operation Righteous Vengeance?

623
00:50:25.692 --> 00:50:26.985
On the Nimitz?

624
00:50:29.863 --> 00:50:31.281
It's usually based in San Diego.

625
00:50:31.365 --> 00:50:34.910
but it's been in Norfolk
since it got back from Iran.

626
00:50:34.993 --> 00:50:35.994
Sam knows someone on base

627
00:50:36.078 --> 00:50:38.247
who's willing to talk to us
off the record.

628
00:50:38.330 --> 00:50:39.873
What changed his mind?

629
00:50:41.750 --> 00:50:43.043
I'm guessing Charlotte.

630
00:50:43.126 --> 00:50:44.753
Just knowing what she means to me.

631
00:50:49.216 --> 00:50:50.259
I know Sam.

632
00:50:50.968 --> 00:50:52.386
We didn't just play in a band together.

633
00:50:52.469 --> 00:50:57.266
We got shot at together.
and I've rarely heard him this scared.

634
00:50:59.935 --> 00:51:02.396
Okay. you think all of this
has to do with AI though?

635
00:51:02.479 --> 00:51:03.897
I don't know.

636
00:51:03.981 --> 00:51:08.402
but the other carrier groups that night
sent out 20. 30 sorties.

637
00:51:08.485 --> 00:51:10.028
and the Nimitz sends out one?

638
00:51:10.112 --> 00:51:13.282
With four planes equipped
with pre-digital comms. and then suddenly...

639
00:51:16.577 --> 00:51:17.578
Jesus.

640
00:51:18.287 --> 00:51:20.747
- Give me a little warning next time.
- That wasn't me.

641
00:51:20.831 --> 00:51:22.249
- What do you mean?
- I mean it wasn't me.

642
00:51:22.332 --> 00:51:24.042
I'm not driving. Someone else is.

643
00:51:25.305 --> 00:52:25.280
Do you want subtitles for any video?
